  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 140 AM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nQuiet weather expected through Thursday night with seasonably \nwarm temperatures and very comfortable humidity levels. Lake \nbreezes both today and tomorrow will result in some modest \ncooling right along the lakefront. While skies should be sunny \ntoday, wildfire smoke aloft will likely filter the sun some.\n\nGuidance continues to bring a strong northern stream shortwave\ntrough into the Midwest Friday. Our area will remain on the cool\nside of the developing surface low, so the better instability\nand thunderstorm chances should remain south of our CWA.\nHowever, strong synoptic ascent and seasonably high PWATs could\nallow for a pretty good soaking for areas that end up under the\ndeformation zone rain Friday night, which looks to be most of\nour CWA. The cloud cover and developing rain on Friday should\nresult in below average temps; mostly in the 70s, except lower\n80s eastern most CWA where rain will arrive last. \n\nLower confidence in the forecast details Saturday as there is\nspread in guidance in how quickly this system moves out. Medium\nrange guidance has trended away from cutting off a mid-upper\nlevel low that meanders around the region and now is more\nprogressive pushing the trough southeast of the area. Timing of\nthe trough's departure will impact rain chances and temperatures\nover the weekend. Given the lower than average forecast\nconfidence, no changes were made to NBM which maintains cooler\ntemps and rain into Saturday. If guidance continues to trend\nquicker, then later Saturday and especially Sunday could end up\ndry. Next week looks to start dry and seasonably warm. \n\n- Izzi",
